nodecode-security-scan is a rewrite of NousResearch's NousResearch/hermes-official-plugins:

  https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-official-plugins
  commit 65f5ad93c7dc14dc661ff2ff3ead0fda71e7bd9d
  Apache-2.0, Copyright (c) 2026 unsupportedpastels (LICENSE; the holder as
  their NOTICE states it), with portions Copyright (c) 2025 OpenAI

Rewritten from Python into Common Lisp against the Nodecode cell contract:
the nine security_scan_* tools (start, get, checkpoint, submit_worker_result,
record_validations, record_chains, finalize, cancel, export) and their
arguments, the /security command and its holder-only validation grants, the
chunked walk with the standard/deep/diff modes and what each skips, the
evidence model (rule, severity, exact path and line, evidence state,
taxonomy, validation status, fingerprint), the rule that a confirmation needs
a passing test and a behaving negative control, and the four exports
(Markdown, canonical findings JSON, SARIF 2.1.0 and formula-escaped CSV). The
OSV dependency check is kept, without the pinned osv-scanner download: the cell
queries api.osv.dev itself.

Left out: the desktop Security page and its dashboard API, the
`hermes security-review` CLI, the subagent pool and its worker leases with the
automatic "Continue security scan" turn injection, the import-map ranking of a
repository over 90 chunks, the seven prose skills, the endoflife.date runtime
check, and the http-probe/local-command execution of validation plans (a plan
can be recorded, and the grant that would allow it minted, but nothing runs
here). The scan store is one JSON file per scan under the home rather than
SQLite: this cell is the only process that writes it, so a database earns
nothing.
